# Server Actions & API Routes Best Practices

## Server Actions

- Define Server Actions in separate `actions.ts` files
- Mark files with 'use server' directive
- Always validate input data with Zod schemas
- Implement proper error handling
- Return serializable data only
- Use revalidatePath() or revalidateTag() for cache updates
- Handle authentication in actions

## Server Action Structure

- Keep actions focused and single-purpose
- Use descriptive action names (e.g., `createUser`, `updateProfile`)
- Validate authentication at the start of each action
- Parse and validate input with Zod
- Use try-catch blocks for error handling
- Return consistent response format (success/error)

## API Routes (Route Handlers)

- Place API routes in `app/api` directory
- Export named functions: GET, POST, PUT, DELETE, PATCH
- Validate request data with Zod schemas
- Return proper HTTP status codes
- Use NextResponse for responses
- Implement proper error handling
- Add authentication checks

## Request Validation

- Validate all incoming data (body, params, query)
- Use Zod schemas for validation
- Return 400 Bad Request for validation errors
- Sanitize input data
- Check Content-Type headers
- Validate file uploads properly

## Response Handling

- Return consistent JSON structure
- Use proper HTTP status codes (200, 201, 400, 401, 403, 404, 500)
- Include error messages in error responses
- Don't expose internal error details to clients
- Use NextResponse.json() for JSON responses
- Set appropriate headers (Content-Type, Cache-Control)

## Authentication & Authorization

- Check auth in every Server Action and API route
- Use Supabase server client for auth checks
- Return 401 for unauthenticated requests
- Return 403 for unauthorized requests
- Validate user permissions
- Handle expired sessions

## Error Handling

- Use try-catch blocks in all actions/routes
- Return user-friendly error messages
- Log errors for monitoring
- Don't expose stack traces to clients
- Handle Supabase errors specifically
- Return proper status codes

## Database Operations

- Use Supabase server client for database access
- Implement proper transaction handling
- Handle database errors gracefully
- Use RLS policies for security
- Validate data before database operations
- Return typed responses

## Performance

- Use streaming responses for large data
- Implement proper caching with revalidate
- Minimize database queries
- Use database indexes effectively
- Implement pagination for large datasets
- Cache frequently accessed data

## Security

- Always validate input data
- Implement rate limiting
- Use CSRF protection
- Validate Content-Type headers
- Sanitize user input
- Use parameterized queries (Supabase handles this)
- Implement proper CORS headers
- Don't expose sensitive data

## Revalidation

- Use revalidatePath() to refresh specific routes
- Use revalidateTag() for tagged cache entries
- Revalidate after mutations
- Use appropriate revalidation strategies
- Handle revalidation errors
- Consider on-demand revalidation

## Testing

- Write unit tests for Server Actions
- Test validation logic thoroughly
- Test error scenarios
- Mock Supabase client in tests
- Test authentication/authorization
- Test edge cases

## Best Practices

- Keep actions simple and focused
- Return serializable data only
- Use TypeScript for type safety
- Implement proper logging
- Handle edge cases gracefully
- Document complex actions
- Use consistent naming conventions
